BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Women's Bikepacking Overnight w/ Earth Mountain!
DTSTART:20260912T110000
DTEND:20260913T150000
DTSTAMP:20260904T133534Z
UID:75f2fce441c009eb@altar.bike
CATEGORIES:trail-work
DESCRIPTION:Women’s Overnight Bikepacking Trip with Earth Mountain! Join
  us for a women’s overnight bikepacking adventure through Pisgah Nationa
 l Forest with Earth Mountain! This bikepacking trip is a great opportunity
  to learn the basics\, spend a night in the woods\, and connect with other
  women who love riding and exploring. The total route is approximately 39 
 miles with 3\,770 feet of climbing \, with about 1\,500 feet of climbing e
 ach day. The route includes options for gravel and single track\, so both 
 gravel and mountain bikes are welcome! Route : Looking Glass Loop Overnigh
 t What to Expect: Bring the good vibes: We're always stoked to be in bikin
 g and camping in the woods\, and even moreso to share it with a rad group 
 of ladies. Bring your own food: You’ll be responsible for bringing your 
 food for th\n\nMore: https://www.pisgahareasorba.org/\n\nSource: Pisgah Ar
 ea SORBA\n\nListed by Altar Cycles — altar.bike/calendar
LOCATION:Jimmy Harris Railroad Depot Park\, Railroad Avenue\, Brevard\, NC
 \, USA\, Brevard\, NC
URL:https://www.pisgahareasorba.org/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NCCX Pre-Season Skills Clinics 2026
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTSTAMP:20260904T133534Z
UID:bbf6b38b2e5ea38d@altar.bike
CATEGORIES:clinic
DESCRIPTION:Learn all about cyclocross and the skills needed to compete wi
 th local experts and pro racers\, as well as get warmed up for the upcomin
 g season! Sessions will allow for new and experienced racers alike to prac
 tice and prepare for racing. Women's only clinic is for female athletes an
 d is focused on beginner and new racers. Limited to 25 participants. Coach
 ed by experienced racers\, including U23 elite racer Ada Watson. Clinic ru
 ns 8am-11am. Attendees are invited to bring a bagged lunch and stay for cr
 afts and conversation. Open clinic is open to all levels of experience\, a
 bilities\, and genders. Guest coaching will be lead by retired pro racer a
 nd certified coach Jon Hamblin and other guest coaches. Please be ready to
  ride at 12pm\, clinic will end at 6pm. Bring a snack for a mid-session br
 eak\n\nMore: http://www.BikeReg.com/nccx-pre-season-skills-clinic-2026\n\n
 Source: BikeReg\n\nListed by Altar Cycles — altar.bike/calendar
GEO:35.508641;-82.6130561
LOCATION:125 Idlewood Dr\, Asheville\, NC
URL:http://www.BikeReg.com/nccx-pre-season-skills-clinic-2026
END:VEVENT
