BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bootlegger
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270417
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270417
DTSTAMP:20260904T133534Z
UID:f0fa19e43a2adce0@altar.bike
CATEGORIES:race
DESCRIPTION:The Bootlegger is one of the most challenging and scenic grave
 l events of the year! There are two route choices (58 and 85 miles) that b
 oth start and finish in downtown Lenoir\, NC and travel through the beauti
 ful and rugged Wilson Creek Gorge. The 58 mile route has approximately 450
 0 feet of climbing while the 85 includes approximately 7250 feet of climbi
 ng. Be sure to keep your head up and enjoy the scenery as the Bootlegger 1
 00 takes you from historic downtown Lenoir and into the heart of the “ot
 her Pisgah\,” also known as the Grandfather Ranger District. Both the 85
  and 58 mile options roll through the countryside before delivering you to
  a gravel wonderland with plenty of challenging terrain. Just after you pa
 ss Coffey’s General Store and Museum\, the two routes split\, and the lo
 ng cours\n\nMore: http://www.BikeReg.com/bootlegger-2027\n\nSource: BikeRe
 g\n\nListed by Altar Cycles — altar.bike/calendar
GEO:35.9132554;-81.5406276
LOCATION:100 Boundary St NW\, Lenoir\, NC
URL:http://www.BikeReg.com/bootlegger-2027
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pisgah Mountain Bike Adventure Race
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270501
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270501
DTSTAMP:20260904T133534Z
UID:996261671a499518@altar.bike
CATEGORIES:race
DESCRIPTION:The Pisgah Mountain Bike Adventure Race (PMBAR) is the absolut
 e pinnacle of MTB Adventure Racing. A mix of brutal and beautiful\, this t
 est of spirit and camaraderie tasks teams of two racers to reach 4 of 5 ch
 eckpoints\, in any order\, and return to the start/finish as fast as possi
 ble. The team with the lowest overall time wins. Checkpoint locations rema
 in secret until start-time and there is no suggested route. Routes vary be
 tween 50-80 miles\, include 9\,000-15\,000 feet of climbing\, and take 7-1
 4 hours to complete. PMBAR is held deep in the Pisgah National Forest\, on
 e of the most beautiful\, rugged\, and unforgiving areas in the nation. Th
 ere will be little to no water or food support on course. Once you leave t
 he start/finish you are on your own. There will be no drops\, sag wagons\,
  or other \n\nMore: http://www.BikeReg.com/pisgah-mountain-bike-adventure-
 race-2027\n\nSource: BikeReg\n\nListed by Altar Cycles — altar.bike/cale
 ndar
GEO:35.2830246;-82.7218935
LOCATION:1284 Pisgah Hwy\, Pisgah Forest\, NC
URL:http://www.BikeReg.com/pisgah-mountain-bike-adventure-race-2027
END:VEVENT
